# Copy to .env and adjust if you need to. Never commit .env.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to client code, and it inlines
# them at BUILD time — not at runtime. A production image therefore has these
# values baked in, which is why nothing secret may ever appear in this file:
# every value here ships to the browser in plain text.

# Base URL every API request is prefixed with (src/shared/api/api-client.ts).
#
# Keep this as the relative path "/api". The frontend and the backend are served
# from the same origin in every environment — Vite's dev server proxies /api to
# the local backend, and in production Caddy proxies /api to the backend
# container. A relative path is what makes the session cookie same-origin, so
# `withCredentials` works and CSRF stays intact. Setting this to an absolute
# cross-origin URL would break authentication.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
